  "prefLabel": "Plc 1902.01 Breastfeeding",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1902.01 “Breastfeeding” means the act of feeding human breast milk to an infant, either directly from the human breast or pumped from the human breast and fed to an infant in a bottle, during the postpartum period.\n\nSource. #14429, eff 1-16-26, EXPIRES 1-16-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1900.html"
